# Lattice iCE40 LP/HX, as much of it as Reticle can state confidently.
#
# Provenance and confidence, stated per group because it differs:
#
#   * Primitive names and ports (SB_LUT4, SB_CARRY, SB_DFF*, SB_IO, SB_GB,
#     SB_RAM40_4K, SB_PLL40_*) come from the SiliconBlue / Lattice iCE
#     Technology Library, which every published iCE40 design and the
#     Yosys `synth_ice40` pass use verbatim. High confidence.
#   * Logic cell: 4-input LUT plus one carry bit plus one flip-flop; the
#     clock, clock enable and set/reset of the eight logic cells in a tile
#     are shared, which is why `shared_reset` is set. High confidence.
#   * The twenty SB_DFF* lines are the whole family, named by the library's
#     own scheme SB_DFF[N][E][S][S|R]: `N` a falling clock edge, `E` a
#     clock enable, a leading `S` a synchronous rather than asynchronous
#     set or reset, and the final `R`/`S` a reset (to 0, pin `R`) or a set
#     (to 1, pin `S`). Both are active high, which is why no variant is
#     marked `active_low`: an active-low reset is inverted in logic
#     first, by one LUT per reset net that flip-flop mapping inserts.
#     `count` is the number of flip-flops on the die and is recorded once,
#     on the plain variant; they are all the same flip-flop configured
#     differently. High confidence.
#   * The four with both an enable and a synchronous set/reset (SB_DFFESR,
#     SB_DFFESS, SB_DFFNESR, SB_DFFNESS) are `enable_gates_reset`: the reset
#     acts only on an enabled edge, `if (E) Q <= R ? 0 : D`. That is the iCE
#     Technology Library's model as Yosys's techlibs/ice40/cells_sim.v writes
#     it (and its ff_map.v maps only $_SDFFCE_*, enable over reset, onto
#     them), and it is how IceStorm's icebox_vlog decodes a configured logic
#     cell, `if (cen) q <= sr ? set : d`. CHECKED on an iCE40UP5K, where a
#     UART echo that relied on the reset winning answered only `00`
#     (docs/fpga-icestorm.md). The asynchronous ones act whatever the enable.
#   * SB_RAM40_4K: 4096 bits, configurable 256x16, 512x8, 1024x4 and
#     2048x2, one read port and one write port with independent clocks,
#     contents initialisable through INIT_0..INIT_F. High confidence.
#     The 16-bit mode has a bit-granular MASK input rather than byte
#     enables, so `byte_enable` is deliberately not set. READ_MODE and
#     WRITE_MODE select the width, 0 for 16 bits through 3 for 2 bits.
#   * SB_RAM40_4K layout, on each `mode` line. The contents are 256 rows
#     of 16 bits, and INIT_<k> holds rows 16k..16k+15, row 16k+i in bits
#     16i+15..16i (`init_params`). HIGH confidence: it is the iCE
#     Technology Library's definition, which the Yosys simulation model
#     and icebox both follow. The row is always address bits 7..0; in a
#     narrow mode the address bits above them pick which word of the row,
#     and word `s` keeps its data bit `j` in row bit (16/width)*j + s
#     (`init high ...`). The narrow modes also move the data pins: 512x8
#     uses WDATA/RDATA 0,2,..,14, 1024x4 uses 1,5,9,13 and 2048x2 uses 3
#     and 11 (`data ...`). Both were first written from memory of the Yosys
#     simulation model of SB_RAM40_4K (write masks selected by WADDR[10:8],
#     data pins spread); that model, read since (techlibs/ice40/cells_sim.v),
#     says exactly this. CHECKED on an iCE40UP5K, the part with the same
#     block RAM: every word of a block RAM in each width, contents from
#     `initial` and written at run time, read back as stated
#     (docs/fpga-icestorm.md). Not checked on an LP or HX part.
#   * SB_IO's PIN_TYPE values below (6'b000001 for a plain input,
#     6'b011001 for a plain output, 6'b101001 for a tristatable one) are
#     the ones every published iCE40 design uses. Medium-high confidence.
#     SB_IO also registers both clock edges itself, which is the iCE40's
#     DDR IO: D_IN_0 / D_IN_1 capture the pad on the rising / falling edge
#     of INPUT_CLK, D_OUT_0 / D_OUT_1 are launched on the rising / falling
#     edge of OUTPUT_CLK. PIN_TYPE 6'b000000 is "no output, input
#     registered" (PIN_INPUT_DDR shares the registered code) and
#     6'b010000 is PIN_OUTPUT_DDR, from the iCE Technology Library's
#     PIN_TYPE table. MEDIUM-HIGH confidence. The family has no
#     programmable IO delay, so none is declared and a request for one is
#     reported.
#   * SB_PLL40_CORE / SB_PLL40_PAD / SB_PLL40_2F_CORE: the ranges
#     (reference 10-133 MHz, phase detector 10-133 MHz, VCO 533-1066 MHz),
#     the fields (DIVR 4 bits storing divisor-1, DIVF 7 bits storing
#     divisor-1, DIVQ 1-6 storing a power of two) and the FILTER_RANGE bands
#     by phase-detector frequency (below 17, 26, 44, 66, 101 MHz, and above)
#     are the ones Project IceStorm's `icepll` uses for SIMPLE feedback, and
#     the solver gives icepll's settings (CHECKED on the UltraPlus line, the
#     same arithmetic). RESETB is active low and tied high, BYPASS tied low.
#     `count` is the number of PLLs the chip database gives the die in that
#     package — its `LOCKED` lines take the 1k's away in the vq100 and the
#     8k's top one in the cm81 — so a part with none has no `pll` line. The
#     PAD form takes its reference straight from a package pin, so its
#     reference is recorded as `pad`, not `ref`. `outglobal`/`outglobalb`
#     are the outputs that drive a global network themselves
#     (PLLOUTGLOBAL*), so mapping puts no buffer behind them.
#   * Since 19 November 2026 every part below is on the REAL FABRIC: Reticle
#     places, routes and writes a bitstream for it on Project IceStorm's chip
#     database (src/fpga/icestorm, docs/fpga-icestorm.md). Every count, pin
#     and grid in this file is that database's, and
#     `every_device_file_is_its_parts_database` (tests/fpga_icestorm.rs)
#     checks each part's file against it. NO LP OR HX PART HAS BEEN ON A
#     BOARD: what was checked is the bits (every one decodes, the arcs are
#     the router's), IceStorm's own decode of them simulated against the
#     source, icepack's bytes and nextpnr's builds of the same designs.
#     ice40-hx1k-tq144 and ice40-lp1k-tq144 also serve the synthetic
#     architecture (src/fpga/arch/synthetic.rs), which a library caller of
#     `place_and_route` still gets and whose tests and goldens are unchanged.
#   * ICESTORM_LC and ICESTORM_LC_COMB are the packed logic cell, as on the
#     UltraPlus below; a design has no reason to instantiate either.
#   * Resource counts — 384 logic cells and no block RAM on the 384, 1280 and
#     16 on the 1k, 7680 and 32 on the 8k — are the chip database's tiles:
#     eight logic cells to a logic tile, a block RAM to a `ramb`/`ramt` pair.
#     CHECKED against it. The HX4K is the 8k die in another package
#     (IceStorm's `tq144:4k`); Lattice's data sheet gives it 3520 logic cells,
#     which its own tools enforce, and nextpnr, like this backend, places on
#     all 7680. QUOTED: no HX4K was on a board.
#   * The tile grid is the chip database's (8 x 10 for the 384, 14 x 18 for
#     the 1k, 34 x 34 for the 8k). HIGH, CHECKED.
#   * No DSP blocks, single-port RAM or oscillators: those exist only on the
#     UltraPlus and iCE40 Ultra parts, and a design instantiating one is
#     told no module of that name exists for this part.
#   * IO: the iCE40 IO buffer has no programmable drive strength or slew
#     rate, so the standards below carry only a bank voltage. The parts
#     have four IO banks (0 top, 1 right, 2 bottom, 3 left), but the chip
#     database does not say which package pin is in which bank, so a single
#     synthetic bank named `io` holds every pin. Do not read the bank name
#     as silicon truth.
#   * PIN LISTS ARE THE WHOLE PACKAGE, from the chip database's `.pins
#     <package>` section (CHECKED by the test above, pin for pin): every
#     ball IceStorm maps to an IO block. The ones that can drive a global
#     network directly (`.gbufpin`) are marked `clock`. Until 19 November
#     2026 these lists were the pins of the boards that use the parts (the
#     iCEstick, the HX8K breakout) and the ct256 one was `pins partial`;
#     every one of those pins is in the lists now, as the same kind.

device ice40-lp384-qn32
  family ice40
  package qn32
  speed lp
  lut_size 4
  ff enable sync_reset async_reset shared_reset init 0
  bel SB_LUT4 lut count 384 port i=I0,I1,I2,I3 o=O param LUT_INIT=16'h0000
  bel SB_CARRY carry port ci=CI i0=I0 i1=I1 co=CO
  bel SB_DFF ff count 384 mode posedge port clk=C d=D q=Q
  bel SB_DFFSR ff mode posedge,sync_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFR ff mode posedge,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFSS ff mode posedge,sync_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFS ff mode posedge,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFE ff mode posedge,enable port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E
  bel SB_DFFESR ff mode posedge,enable,sync_reset,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFER ff mode posedge,enable,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFESS ff mode posedge,enable,sync_set,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel SB_DFFES ff mode posedge,enable,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel SB_DFFN ff mode negedge port clk=C d=D q=Q
  bel SB_DFFNSR ff mode negedge,sync_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNR ff mode negedge,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNSS ff mode negedge,sync_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFNS ff mode negedge,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFNE ff mode negedge,enable port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E
  bel SB_DFFNESR ff mode negedge,enable,sync_reset,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNER ff mode negedge,enable,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNESS ff mode negedge,enable,sync_set,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel SB_DFFNES ff mode negedge,enable,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel ICESTORM_LC other site lc port i=I0,I1,I2,I3 cin=CIN cout=COUT o=O clk=CLK en=CEN rst=SR outputs O,COUT param LUT_INIT=16'h0000 CARRY_ENABLE=1'b0 DFF_ENABLE=1'b0 SET_NORESET=1'b0 ASYNC_SR=1'b0 NEG_CLK=1'b0
  bel ICESTORM_LC_COMB other site lcc port i=I0,I1,I2,I3 cin=CIN cout=COUT o=O outputs O,COUT param LUT_INIT=16'h0000 CARRY_ENABLE=1'b0 DFF_ENABLE=1'b0 SET_NORESET=1'b0 ASYNC_SR=1'b0 NEG_CLK=1'b0
  bel SB_IO io port pad=PACKAGE_PIN din=D_IN_0 dout=D_OUT_0 oe=OUTPUT_ENABLE din1=D_IN_1 dout1=D_OUT_1 iclk=INPUT_CLK oclk=OUTPUT_CLK ce=CLOCK_ENABLE param_in PIN_TYPE=6'b000001 param_out PIN_TYPE=6'b011001 param_inout PIN_TYPE=6'b101001 param_pullup PULLUP=1 param_ddr_in PIN_TYPE=6'b000000 param_ddr_out PIN_TYPE=6'b010000
  bel SB_GB gb count 8 port i=USER_SIGNAL_TO_GLOBAL_BUFFER o=GLOBAL_BUFFER_OUTPUT
  io_standard LVCMOS33 vccio 3.3
  io_standard LVCMOS25 vccio 2.5
  io_standard LVCMOS18 vccio 1.8
  io_standard SB_LVDS_INPUT vccio 2.5 differential
  bank io vccio 3.3,2.5,1.8
  pin 1 io bank io
  pin 2 io bank io
  pin 5 io bank io
  pin 6 clock bank io
  pin 7 io bank io
  pin 8 clock bank io
  pin 12 io bank io
  pin 13 io bank io
  pin 14 io bank io
  pin 15 io bank io
  pin 18 io bank io
  pin 19 clock bank io
  pin 20 clock bank io
  pin 22 io bank io
  pin 23 io bank io
  pin 26 io bank io
  pin 27 io bank io
  pin 29 clock bank io
  pin 30 clock bank io
  pin 31 io bank io
  pin 32 io bank io
  global_buffers 8
  clock_region global 0 0 7 9
  grid 8 10
end

device ice40-lp1k-tq144
  family ice40
  package tq144
  speed lp
  lut_size 4
  ff enable sync_reset async_reset shared_reset init 0
  bel SB_LUT4 lut count 1280 port i=I0,I1,I2,I3 o=O param LUT_INIT=16'h0000
  bel SB_CARRY carry port ci=CI i0=I0 i1=I1 co=CO
  bel SB_DFF ff count 1280 mode posedge port clk=C d=D q=Q
  bel SB_DFFSR ff mode posedge,sync_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFR ff mode posedge,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFSS ff mode posedge,sync_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFS ff mode posedge,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFE ff mode posedge,enable port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E
  bel SB_DFFESR ff mode posedge,enable,sync_reset,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFER ff mode posedge,enable,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFESS ff mode posedge,enable,sync_set,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel SB_DFFES ff mode posedge,enable,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel SB_DFFN ff mode negedge port clk=C d=D q=Q
  bel SB_DFFNSR ff mode negedge,sync_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNR ff mode negedge,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNSS ff mode negedge,sync_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFNS ff mode negedge,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q rst=S
  bel SB_DFFNE ff mode negedge,enable port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E
  bel SB_DFFNESR ff mode negedge,enable,sync_reset,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNER ff mode negedge,enable,async_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=R
  bel SB_DFFNESS ff mode negedge,enable,sync_set,enable_gates_reset port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel SB_DFFNES ff mode negedge,enable,async_set port clk=C d=D q=Q en=E rst=S
  bel ICESTORM_LC other site lc port i=I0,I1,I2,I3 cin=CIN cout=COUT o=O clk=CLK en=CEN rst=SR outputs O,COUT param LUT_INIT=16'h0000 CARRY_ENABLE=1'b0 DFF_ENABLE=1'b0 SET_NORESET=1'b0 ASYNC_SR=1'b0 NEG_CLK=1'b0
  bel ICESTORM_LC_COMB other site lcc port i=I0,I1,I2,I3 cin=CIN cout=COUT o=O outputs O,COUT param LUT_INIT=16'h0000 CARRY_ENABLE=1'b0 DFF_ENABLE=1'b0 SET_NORESET=1'b0 ASYNC_SR=1'b0 NEG_CLK=1'b0
  bel SB_IO io port pad=PACKAGE_PIN din=D_IN_0 dout=D_OUT_0 oe=OUTPUT_ENABLE din1=D_IN_1 dout1=D_OUT_1 iclk=INPUT_CLK oclk=OUTPUT_CLK ce=CLOCK_ENABLE param_in PIN_TYPE=6'b000001 param_out PIN_TYPE=6'b011001 param_inout PIN_TYPE=6'b101001 param_pullup PULLUP=1 param_ddr_in PIN_TYPE=6'b000000 param_ddr_out PIN_TYPE=6'b010000
  bel SB_GB gb count 8 port i=USER_SIGNAL_TO_GLOBAL_BUFFER o=GLOBAL_BUFFER_OUTPUT
  bram SB_RAM40_4K
    ports 2
    mode 16 256 param READ_MODE=0 WRITE_MODE=0 init high 0-15
    mode 8 512 param READ_MODE=1 WRITE_MODE=1 data 0,2,4,6,8,10,12,14 init high 0,2,4,6,8,10,12,14 1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15
    mode 4 1024 param READ_MODE=2 WRITE_MODE=2 data 1,5,9,13 init high 0,4,8,12 1,5,9,13 2,6,10,14 3,7,11,15
    mode 2 2048 param READ_MODE=3 WRITE_MODE=3 data 3,11 init high 0,8 1,9 2,10 3,11 4,12 5,13 6,14 7,15
    flags dual_port init
    init_params INIT_ count 16 digits 1 rows 16 slot 16
    port read clk=RCLK en=RE addr=RADDR dout=RDATA ce=RCLKE
    port write clk=WCLK en=WE addr=WADDR din=WDATA ce=WCLKE
  end
  io_standard LVCMOS33 vccio 3.3
  io_standard LVCMOS25 vccio 2.5
  io_standard LVCMOS18 vccio 1.8
  io_standard SB_LVDS_INPUT vccio 2.5 differential
  bank io vccio 3.3,2.5,1.8
  pin 1 io bank io
  pin 2 io bank io
  pin 3 io bank io
